bar with its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorModel\/documentation\/IvorModel\/Meter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Bars of that meter follow one another until the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"next entry; if the bar that the next entry falls in is cut off before it reaches its full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"length, it’s a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"short bar"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". An entry with the same meter as the one before it, which doesn’t","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fall on a barline the earlier entry would have drawn anyway, is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"restart"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":": it exists to make","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the bar before it short. A free meter’s whole span, up to the next entry, is one bar with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pulse. Before the first entry there are no bars.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorModel\/documentation\/IvorModel\/MeterTable\/pickup","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is the length of an opening part-bar, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"bar 0","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", when the first entry is a metered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"meter at time 0. Its beats are counted as the tail of a full bar: a one-beat pickup in 3\/4 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"beat 3. Bars are numbered from 1, starting after the pickup, and every later bar — short or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"free — adds 1."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unlike the parameter maps, a meter table never interpolates, and unlike the other tables, it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lives on the work, not on a part, and only in beat time. Its invariants hold after every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mutating method, and decoding rejects a table that breaks them:"}]},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"There’s at most one entry per beat time.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The pickup is 0 unless there’s an entry at time 0 with a metered meter.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The pickup is shorter than that meter’s bar length, and ends no later than the second"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entry, if there is one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormodel\/metertable"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorModel\/SK","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/Sl","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/Se","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/SE","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/Sk","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/IvorModel\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A beat-time table of meters: where each meter takes effect, and the pickup before the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"full bar."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorModel\/documentation\/IvorModel"]]},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorModel\/documentation\/IvorModel\/MeterTable","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorModel/documentation/IvorModel/MeterTable/insert(beatTime:meter:extras:)":{"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormodel\/metertable\/insert(beattime:meter:extras:)","title":"insert(beatTime:meter:extras:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind